Database migrations (Alembic).

RULE: every schema change is a migration. Never edit a table by hand and never call
Base.metadata.create_all(). If you change app/models.py, create a migration in the same pull request.

Common commands (run from the platform/ folder, with the virtual environment active):

  alembic upgrade head                                          apply all migrations
  alembic current                                               show the database's revision
  alembic revision --autogenerate --rev-id 0002 -m "what"       draft a new migration
  alembic check                                                 fail if models and migrations disagree
  alembic downgrade -1                                          undo the last migration (dev only)

Always read an autogenerated migration before committing it: autogenerate misses some changes
(for example renamed columns appear as a drop plus an add).
